From 2e67d0a83a56d817b3e2650b64743edb85b0061e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:10:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/42] fix(harbor_agent): a reply counts as cut by the context
 only near the context limit

0037 counted a reply with finish_reason length as cut by the context
ceiling when it had fewer tokens than the output limit, or when prompt
+ reply reached model_info.max_input_tokens, and then ended the episode
as a context overflow. The first condition also fires far from the
ceiling: the NeMo-RL Apertus 2 chat endpoint reports length for any
output without a reply frame (apply_apertus2_output_to_chat_response_
choices), and vLLM's own length needs max_tokens = min(requested,
max_model_len - len(prompt)) to be reached. In job 5365870 0037 ended
73 episodes this way; at least 22 had prompt + reply well below 24576
even with one token per observation character (one first call: 1163
prompt + 232 reply tokens, then labelled "prompt does not fit" and the
rollout masked although its 7 siblings scored 6 x 1.0).

New rule: a length reply is cut by the context only if prompt +
completion (server usage, else token ids) is within max(256, 1% of the
limit) tokens of max_input_tokens. The clamp makes a real cut end at
the limit exactly; the margin absorbs tokens counted on one side only.
Any other length reply is an ordinary truncation (truncation_retry
resample, then max_consecutive_truncations). Without the prompt size or
the limit it is not a cut. Both errors now carry the numbers ("P prompt
+ C completion = T tokens; output limit O, context limit L").

"prompt does not fit" is now used only when the model server rejected
the first prompt itself (Gym's fake response; in 5365870 the 60 fake
responses match the endpoint's 60 "Prompt length (24582-24615) fills
or exceeds" warnings): NemoGymLLM sets prompt_over_context_limit and
Terminus2NemoGym writes it to agent_error_flags.json. Flags written
before this change fall back to "no context cut on the first call".

Offline replay over 5365870 (prompt of the cut call not recorded;
bounds from the last answered call's usage and the next observation):
of 0037's 73 cuts, 22 are cuts under the new rule, 22 are not, 29
depend on the observation's token count (point estimate at 3 chars per
token: 45 cut, 28 not).

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
